th minimal potential. With only 1 remaining in unshown tiles, the probability of drawing another W8 to form a pair is extremely low. Additionally, W8 cannot connect with any of my other tiles to form chows. By discarding W8, I maintain my four existing pairs (W1, T1, T7, B1) and keep tiles that have better potential for forming additional pairs or chows (like T2-T3-T4, T6-T7-T8, B1-B2-B3). This keeps my hand flexible for both Seven Pairs and standard winning patterns.\n\nAnswer: Play W8"}
